  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"280\">A <strong data-start=\"57\" data-end=\"90\">nighttime (PM) cortisol level</strong> is measured to evaluate the <strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"140\">diurnal variation</strong> of cortisol secretion, which is important for diagnosing disorders related to <strong data-start=\"219\" data-end=\"239\">adrenal function</strong> or <strong data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"267\">pituitary regulation</strong>, especially:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"282\" data-end=\"354\">\n<li data-start=\"282\" data-end=\"306\">\n<p data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"306\"><strong data-start=\"284\" data-end=\"306\">Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"307\" data-end=\"354\">\n<p data-start=\"309\" data-end=\"354\"><strong data-start=\"309\" data-end=\"354\">Adrenal insufficiency (Addison&rsquo;s disease)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Cortisol (Night sample)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low (&lt;5 &micro;g/dL or &lt;140 nmol/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Normal &ndash; expected suppression at night</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Borderline (5&ndash;10 &micro;g/dL or 140&ndash;275 nmol/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Indeterminate &ndash; may warrant further testing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High (&gt;10 &micro;g/dL or &gt;275 nmol/L)</strong></td>\n<td>Abnormal &ndash; suggests loss of diurnal variation; <strong>possible Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Conditions Indicated by Abnormal Night Cortisol</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Expected Night Cortisol</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal individual</strong></td>\n<td>Suppressed (low)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</strong></td>\n<td>Elevated</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Adrenal insufficiency</strong></td>\n<td>Low or undetectable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Shift workers / stress</strong></td>\n<td>May show mild elevation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
